<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov nickel imports down 20.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov nickel imports down 20.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined nickel imports fell 20.5 percent to 4,376 tonnes in November from 5,502 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Thursday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (on a customs-cleared basis, in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Nov 96	 Oct 96	Nov 95</p>
<p> Total	   4,376	  4,716	 5,502</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Russia	    401	    657	 1,667</p>
<p> S. Africa	  60	    310	   534</p>
<p> Zimbabwe	  657	    757	   521</p>
<p>Imports in the first 11 months of 1996 totalled 50,573 tonnes, down from 65,673 tonnes in the same period the previous year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
